# Scripts (be selective)
#
# `*.sh` has no leading slash, so it matches at ANY depth — the same mistake
# documented for backend/tests below. It was meant to keep ad-hoc shell scripts
# out of the repo ROOT, but it also ignores scripts/, which is where the
# deliberate ones live. Five files in there are tracked only because they
# predate the rule; the next one added simply vanished, with `git status`
# reporting nothing.
*.sh
!start_backend.sh
!scripts/*.sh

# Ad-hoc test scripts in the repo ROOT only (test_groq_connection.py etc).
# The leading slash matters: without it git matches at ANY depth, which
# silently ignored every new file under backend/tests/. The 19 tracked test
# files there predate the rule; anything added after it vanished from
# `git add` without a word.
/test_*.py
-integra-markets/
-integra-markets-backup/
.vercel
.env

# Raw live schema pulled for SDK regeneration — openapi.json is the filtered
# artefact that gets committed, not this.
live_openapi.json

# Handoff daemon state: pidfile, log, last-write stamp.
# Local runtime, not shared — and without this the daemon reports its own
# state directory as an untracked change in every report it writes.
.handoff/
